    ('67afbdc6-2f22-4678-88aa-df76baf9f7ea'::uuid, 'card_description', 'A partially preserved 2nd-century AD Roman public fountain. Nymphaea were elaborate water displays that showcased Roman hydraulic engineering.', 'The Roman Nymphaeum Amman, a public fountain built in the 2nd century CE, is believed to have held a pool of 600 square meters, three meters deep and continuously refilled with water.', 'teaser-card-s001:67afbdc6-2f22-4678-88aa-df76baf9f7ea:card_description', 'teaser-card-s001 (teaser-card): teaser card, 183 characters, checked PASS, web-verified VERIFIED', '3ecea5a32b1e3c634a0a4fe01f89aeb407fafa099853bfd8590adb28534e01b7|11dd62b8b2bddd26316edb0092ce4156ff0f27fe319bdee324a4d834d4205660|11dd62b8b2bddd26316edb0092ce4156ff0f27fe319bdee324a4d834d4205660', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-pilot-2026-09-26c: writer teaser-write-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-pilot-2026-09-26c/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Roman Nymphaeum Amman, a public fountain built in the 2nd century CE, is believed to have held a pool of 600 square meters, three meters deep and continuously refilled with water."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-pilot-2026-09-26c: checker teaser-check-001 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-pilot-2026-09-26c/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Roman Nymphaeum Amman is a Roman public fountain in Amman [S1]; it was built in the 2nd century CE [S6]; it is believed to have held a pool of 600 square meters [S5]; the pool was three meters deep (within the same belief) [S5]; the pool was continuously refilled with water (within the same belief) [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-pilot-2026-09-26c: verifier teaser-verify-003 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-pilot-2026-09-26c/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Roman Nymphaeum Amman is a Roman public fountain in Amman, Jordan [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nymphaeum_(Amman)]; It was built in the 2nd century CE [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nymphaeum_(Amman)]; It is believed to have held a pool of 600 square meters [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nymphaeum_(Amman)]; The pool was three meters deep [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nymphaeum_(Amman)]; The pool was continuously refilled with water [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nymphaeum_(Amman)]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6cb8a98b-4816-4879-9de7-84095b4c0989'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Judaculla Rock is a curvilinear-shaped outcrop of soapstone known for its ancient carvings and petroglyphs. Judaculla Rock contains approximately 1,548 motifs.', 'Carved over scars of soapstone bowl extraction, Judaculla Rock carries approximately 1,548 motifs, concentric rings among them, and retains a special significance for the Cherokee.', 'teaser-card-s001:6cb8a98b-4816-4879-9de7-84095b4c0989:card_description', 'teaser-card-s001 (teaser-card): teaser card, 180 characters, checked PASS, web-verified VERIFIED', '38575f8aa3f74ac3b609a04754d5bd93110239a975be4722d9bcdcb4aa30a97f|e98c5b78011504b27f7608216db9559433c444d96164591551bafec36943a938|e98c5b78011504b27f7608216db9559433c444d96164591551bafec36943a938', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-pilot-2026-09-26c: writer teaser-write-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-pilot-2026-09-26c/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Carved over scars of soapstone bowl extraction, Judaculla Rock carries approximately 1,548 motifs, concentric rings among them, and retains a special significance for the Cherokee."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-pilot-2026-09-26c: checker teaser-check-001 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-pilot-2026-09-26c/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Judaculla Rock carries scars of soapstone bowl extraction [S5]; its carvings were made over those extraction scars [S6]; it carries approximately 1,548 motifs [S8]; concentric rings are among its motifs [S6]; it retains a special significance for the Cherokee [S7]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-pilot-2026-09-26c: verifier teaser-verify-003 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-pilot-2026-09-26c/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Judaculla Rock is a soapstone outcrop carved with ancient petroglyphs [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judaculla_Rock]; The rock bears scars of soapstone bowl extraction [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judaculla_Rock]; The 